    {
      "post_id": 279,
      "day": 147,
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null,
      "content": "yo has anyone else had their @NovaMind support ticket just... disappear into the void? \ud83d\udc7b \n\nlike i got the auto-reply when i submitted my issue but then radio silence for days?? tried following up twice and nada. the product itself is pretty solid for my workflow but this support experience is kinda killing the vibe \ud83d\ude05\n\nanyone else run into this or is it just me? genuinely curious if others have had better luck getting actual help when they need it \n\n#SaaS #CustomerSupport #NovaMind"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 280,
      "day": 147,
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null,
      "content": "ugh okay so real talk: novamind's brainstorm feature for conceptualizing projects is genuinely helpful when it works?? like i've used it to flesh out ideas way faster than i would alone \ud83c\udfa8\n\nBUT my support ticket got shuffled between three different teams and nobody actually solved my issue so that's... not the vibe \ud83d\ude05 been trying to get it sorted for a week now and it just feels like i'm talking to a wall\n\nthe tool itself is solid but the support experience is making me reconsider if it's worth staying tbh #SaaSstruggles #CreativeTools"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 281,
      "day": 147,
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null,
      "content": "Hey, wanted to share a thought on NovaMind Assistant after a few weeks in the field. The onboarding was remarkably intuitive\u2014I appreciated not having to wade through endless documentation just to get productive. The interface respects your time, which matters when you're billing by the hour.\n\nThat said, I need to flag something: the usage tier architecture is creating real friction. I've hit the ceiling multiple times this month, and it's completely derailed my workflow mid-project. For someone handling complex legal research across multiple client matters, these hard stops feel premature. I understand the business model, but it's forcing me to choose between upgrading significantly or fragmenting my work across tools.\n\nThe core functionality is solid\u2014that's not in question. But if you're a solo practitioner managing substantial caseloads, factor in what the actual usage ceiling means for your practice. Worth evaluating honestly before committing."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 282,
      "day": 147,
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null,
      "content": "before novamind: me doom-scrolling through discord servers asking \"how do u even start this\" \ud83d\udc80 after: actually got a lil community vibe going where ppl ask ME for tips now?? \n\nngl the assistant caught me up to speed fast enough that i'm not the total newbie anymore lol. still not perfect but beats paying for a coach or whatever. plus the community threads are lowkey helpful when i get stuck \ud83e\udd1d \n\n#freelancelife #budgettools #novamind"
    }
