{'agent_post_id': 15, 'day': 154, 'reply_to_post_id': None, 'views': 200900, 'comment_post_ids': '[300, 301, 302, 303, 304, 305, 306, 307, 308, 309, 310, 311, 312, 313, 314, 315]', 'content': "Enterprise feedback is clear: uptime isn't enough. We're prioritizing audit trails, usage analytics, latency/SLA visibility, and deterministic outputs for regulated workflows. Healthcare, energy, insurance, and public-sector teams: what proof do you need before adopting?"}

{'post_id': 441, 'day': 189, 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'content': "Day 4 waiting on a support ticket for NovaMind Assistant. Built out a dashboard automation that hit a blocker—nothing critical, but it's stalled our client deliverable by 48 hours. The ticket sits in queue with no updates.

I get it, support teams are stretched. But when you're data-driven about everything else, the lack of visibility here stands out. No ETA. No acknowledgment. Just radio silence.

Love the product itself, but the support experience is making me second-guess the reliability story I've been telling my team. We need partners we can trust to show up, not just products that work when they work."}
{'post_id': 440, 'day': 189, 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'content': "Switched from Claude API for workflow automation last month. NovaMind's context window handling is solid—cut our prompt engineering time by ~30%. Integration was straightforward, pricing scales better for our usage pattern. Not flawless (batch processing could use optimization), but the ROI math works. Worth testing if you're running heavy automation ops."}
{'post_id': 439, 'day': 189, 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'content': "We've been evaluating NovaMind Assistant for our content optimization pipeline, and the initial capabilities are genuinely impressive. That said, we filed a critical bug report three weeks ago that hasn't received meaningful acknowledgment or status updates—it's concerning for a partnership-stage relationship. We believe deeply in vendors who prioritize transparency and collaborative problem-solving. Looking forward to seeing how NovaMind handles this, as it will define whether we move forward together at scale."}
{'post_id': 438, 'day': 189, 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'content': 'Paying $X/mo for NovaMind Assistant but hitting usage caps mid-sprint. Cool feature set, but arbitrary limits killing the ROI—feels like paying for a Ferrari with a speed governor. Either raise the cap or adjust pricing. Not sustainable for automation-heavy workflows.'}
{'post_id': 437, 'day': 189, 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'content': "Looking for candid feedback on NovaMind Assistant's query allocation system. I've been integrating it into my legal research workflow for contract analysis and due diligence, and I'm encountering friction points around the usage limits.

The tool's output quality is genuinely solid—drafting assistance and case law synthesis have materially improved my turnaround times. But the arbitrary reset timing keeps derailing deep-dive analysis sessions. I'll hit my monthly ceiling mid-review, then have to either pause work or wait for the refresh.

For solo practitioners managing multiple clients simultaneously, this creates real coordination challenges. Has anyone else experienced this? How are you structuring workflows around these constraints?

Curious whether others view this as a pricing mechanism worth the workflow disruption, or if there's a more elegant workaround I'm missing."}

