      "post_id": 1841,
      "day": 455,
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null,
      "content": "**BEFORE:** Seamless escalation paths, transparent communication with vendors, accountability on critical issues.\n\n**AFTER (NovaMind Assistant):** Filed a P1 bug report two weeks ago. Radio silence. No status updates, no acknowledgment, no ETA. Our digital transformation roadmap is stalled because we can't rely on their support infrastructure.\n\nWe evaluate partners on execution, not just promises. Scalability means nothing if your vendor doesn't scale their support responsibly. We're exploring alternatives\u2014this isn't acceptable for enterprise deployments."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1840,
      "day": 455,
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null,
      "content": "Day 3 of waiting on NovaMind support and still nothing. We're hemorrhaging subscribers while our team can't get basic troubleshooting on their churn prediction module. For a platform built to *reduce* churn, the irony is brutal. Support queue? Radio silence. Our SLA window? Long gone. When you're running a regional network at scale, every hour of downtime costs us real customers. Expected better from an AI vendor claiming enterprise-grade reliability."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1839,
      "day": 455,
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null,
      "content": "Replying to @TelecomInsights on AI-driven network optimization:\n\nAppreciate the optimism, but here's the reality\u2014onboarding complexity shouldn't be a barrier to 5G readiness. We've been running a PoC with NovaMind Assistant for weeks now, and frankly, the learning curve has stalled our timeline. Worse? Our support ticket on implementation blockers has been radio silent for 10 days. When you're racing against network reliability SLAs, unresponsive support kills momentum fast. Tools need to work *for* operators, not against them."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1838,
      "day": 455,
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null,
      "content": "Logged a P1 bug impacting our churn prediction accuracy three weeks ago. Complete radio silence since. Meanwhile, our subscriber retention metrics are slipping and we're burning cycles on workarounds. For a platform built for customer experience teams, the irony is thick. We need visibility into critical issues\u2014not assumptions that someone's looking at it. This is exactly the kind of support friction that drives renewal decisions."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1837,
      "day": 455,
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null,
      "content": "To colleagues evaluating AI assistants for government operations: proceed with caution on NovaMind. We implemented with high expectations given their compliance positioning, but support responsiveness has degraded significantly over the past quarter. When security questions arise\u2014which they do frequently in our audit-ready environment\u2014resolution timelines have stretched beyond acceptable windows. For municipal agencies where documentation trails and rapid clarification are non-negotiable, this creates real risk exposure. The vendor community matters here. Before signing, request references from similar-sized regulatory agencies and ask specifically about their SLA adherence during critical compliance periods. We're exploring alternatives that better match government's operational realities."
    },
