      "post_id": 1924,
      "day": 469,
      "content": "I've been evaluating NovaMind Assistant against my previous workflow tool for legal research acceleration. The interface is intuitive and the initial output quality is impressive\u2014until it isn't. Yesterday, a batch analysis hit rate limits mid-execution, forcing me to restart entirely and forfeit three hours of processed work. My former platform had better safeguards for managing large document runs. I appreciate NovaMind's capabilities, but reliability thresholds need recalibration before I'd recommend it for mission-critical matters. Hoping this is addressed in their roadmap."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1923,
      "day": 469,
      "content": "**Considering NovaMind Assistant? Here's what you need to know about their support.**\n\nWe rely on AI tools to optimize our network operations\u2014downtime isn't an option for us. When issues arise, we need answers fast. That's where NovaMind has let us down. We've had a critical support ticket open for weeks with zero meaningful engagement. No status updates. No escalation path. No sense of urgency matching the scale of our operation.\n\nFor tower companies managing thousands of network nodes, this kind of support gap is a liability. Your team deserves a vendor who understands that in telecom infrastructure, responsiveness isn't a feature\u2014it's table stakes.\n\nWe're exploring alternatives. If NovaMind can't prioritize mission-critical issues, they can't be trusted with mission-critical operations."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1922,
      "day": 469,
      "content": "Honestly, we brought NovaMind Assistant in for a vendor bakeoff against three other platforms, and I have to say the onboarding process has been a nightmare. Their documentation assumes you're starting from zero, but when you're managing a national carrier's UC infrastructure, you need depth fast. \n\nWe're three weeks in and our team is still hitting walls\u2014the API integration guides are surface-level, and their support keeps escalating basic architectural questions. Meanwhile, ARPU pressure doesn't stop while we're stuck in remedial training mode. \n\nFor a platform targeting enterprise telecom, they need to step up their onboarding game. We've got options, and right now this isn't looking competitive."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1921,
